.TH AMBER-BENCH 1 "October 2026" "amber" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amber-bench \- benchmark and KPI harness for amber
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amber-bench
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amber-bench
runs scenario suites against the harness and scores the result. Hermetic runs use
a deterministic fake model, so they are safe in CI; live runs target any
OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
.PP
Scenarios are JSON files at \fI<data>/scenarios/<suite>/<name>.json\fR.
\fI<data>\fR is the install-time data directory, then
\fI<prefix>/share/amber-bench\fR beside the executable, then \fI./bench\fR, so
both an installed package and a source checkout work.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List the available scenarios.
.TP
.B run
Run scenarios. Hermetic by default; \fB\-\-live\fR uses a real endpoint.
.TP
.B validate\-template \fIscenario\fR
Prove that a coding template's hidden tests pass.
.TP
.B report \fIresults.json\fR...
Re-render stored JSON reports. Two or more files render a model comparison.
.TP
.B delta \fIa.json\fR \fIb.json\fR
Report win, lose and stagnate per scenario.
.TP
.B scorecard \fIresults.json\fR
Full diagnostic: dimensions, per-suite breakdown, failed-scenario diagnosis.
.TP
.B calibrate \fIresults.json\fR...
Reference-anchored calibration: headroom, anchor deviation, suggested
difficulties.
.TP
.B reap\-state
Remove old scenario state. A dry run unless \fB\-\-apply\fR is given.
.TP
.B shape\-replay \fIlog.jsonl\fR...
Replay recorded sessions through a context shaper and report tokens saved and
how often a dropped span is referenced later.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-suite \fIname\fR
Restrict to one suite.
.TP
.B \-\-scenario \fIname\fR
Run a single scenario.
.TP
.B \-\-live
Use the real model instead of the hermetic fake.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIname\fR
Model profile from \fIprofiles.json\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-model \fIname\fR
Model override for a live run.
.TP
.B \-\-temperature \fIt\fR
Temperature override for a live run.
.TP
.B \-\-repeat \fIn\fR
Run each scenario \fIn\fR times.
.TP
.B \-\-repeat\-gap\-ms \fIms\fR
Pause between repeats, for endpoints that throttle.
.TP
.B \-\-cat \fIname\fR
Category filter: \fBmodel\fR, \fBharness\fR or \fBboth\fR (default).
.TP
.B \-\-out \fIfile\fR
Write the JSON report to \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIfmt\fR
Report format: \fBtext\fR (default), \fBmarkdown\fR or \fBjson\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-older\-than\-days \fIn\fR
Age floor for \fBreap\-state\fR (default 7, minimum 1).
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Make \fBreap\-state\fR actually remove state.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/amber-bench/scenarios/
The installed scenario corpus, one directory per suite.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amber-bench/profiles.json
Named model profiles used by \fB\-\-profile\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMBER_API_BASE, AMBER_API_KEY, AMBER_MODEL
Endpoint settings for \fB\-\-live\fR runs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amber (1),
.BR amber-cli (1)
